xnu 0186: expand CP_SET_DRAW_STATE groups into register writes

The CP never completes a stream that loads a draw-state group. Measured on the
phone: a 71-dword stream without one writes its fence in 12 ms, while a
168-dword stream carrying a 27-group CP_SET_DRAW_STATE reads its whole IB
(CP_IB1_REM_SIZE 0, CP_IB2_REM_SIZE 0) and never fences, and that stall then
blocks every later submission too -- the UI runs at 2 fps with each frame
waiting the full 5.7 s, drawn in place but never presented.

A group is a list of register/value pairs in GPU memory and the CP does execute
those when they arrive as type-4 register writes (the same submission's other
packets are exactly that). Expand each group into register-write packets, in a
scratch buffer, and submit that stream instead; runs of ascending registers are
batched into one packet. gpunostate=1 keeps the old behaviour for bisection.

